Problem Statement
You are given an integer array arr containing N elements and an integer target.

Your task is to find the total number of triplets whose sum is strictly less than the given target.

A triplet consists of three elements at different indices i, j, and k, such that: i < j < k < N
A triplet is valid if:  arr[i]+arr[j]+arr[k] < target

For Example :
If ‘N’ = 7, ‘ARR’ = { 1, 5, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7 } and ‘TARGET’ = 9

Then, there are three triplets with sum less than 9:
1) {1, 5, 2}
2) {1, 2, 3}
3) {1, 2, 4}
4) {1, 3, 4}

Thus, the output will be 4.

Approach: Brute force
T.C: O(N^3) S.C: O(1)

	public static int threeSumSmaller(int n, int[] arr, int target) {
		// Write your code here.
		   int count = 0;
       for(int i=0;i<n-2;i++){
           for(int j=i+1;j<n-1;j++){
               for(int k=j+1;k<n;k++){
                   if(arr[i]+arr[j]+arr[k]<target){
                       count++;
                   }
               }
           }
       }
       return count;
	}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Approach: Sorting + Two pointer
T.C : O(nlogn) + o(n^2) = O(N^2) S.C: O(1)

public static int threeSumSmaller(int n, int[] arr, int target) {
		// Write your code here.
		int count = 0;
        int sum =  0;

        Arrays.sort(arr);

        for(int i=0;i<n-2;i++){
           int left = i+1;
           int right = n-1;

           while(left<right){
               sum = arr[i]+arr[left]+arr[right];
               if(sum<target){
                   count += right -left;
                   left++;
               }
               else{
                   right--;
               }
           }

        }
    return count;
}
